# What must never enter the production image.
#
# Two jobs. The first is keeping secrets and local state out of a build context
# that gets shipped to a build server and baked into layers - a `.env` copied
# into an image is a credential leak that survives every later `rm`. The second
# is keeping the image small and the build fast.
#
# This file is NOT a duplicate of .gitignore. .gitignore keeps things out of
# Git; this keeps things out of a running container, and the two lists differ:
# `frontend/` is committed and belongs in Git but has no business in a backend
# image, while `.venv/` is in neither.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and local environment - the reason this file exists
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Version control and CI
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Python state
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A host virtualenv holds platform-specific binaries. Copying one into a Linux
# image ships megabytes of Windows or macOS wheels that cannot run there.
.venv
venv
ENV
__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov
coverage.xml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The frontend
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This image runs the Django API. The React bundle is built and hosted
# separately - see docs/deployment.md. node_modules alone would dwarf
# everything else in the context.
frontend

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded and sample images
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uploaded label photographs are third-party content: trade dress, and
# sometimes incidental personal data. A developer's local uploads must not be
# baked into a deployed image where they would be served to other people.
backend/media
samples
uploads

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerated inside the image by `collectstatic`. Copying a host build in
# would let a stale manifest win over the one the build produces.
backend/staticfiles
build
dist
ml/build
ml/dist

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ML data and artifacts
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation photographs and any model weights. Nothing at runtime reads these;
# `ml/labelextract` is the only part of ml/ the container needs, and it is
# installed as a package.
ml/data
ml/artifacts
ml/models
ml/tests
ml/.pytest_cache

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `rules/` is deliberately NOT here. It is read at runtime by load_rules and
# load_legal_framework, not documentation - see the Dockerfile.
docs

# Root-level prose only. A bare `*.md` pattern matches one path segment, so
# this leaves rules/*.md alone - which is what we want: those sit beside the
# JSON the loaders read, and separating them would make the directory harder
# to reason about for no gain in image size.
*.md
